@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280

title Provider detail — a VIEW / MEMBER of the individualProvider page, NOT a page\nOpening one provider on the same terms as a facility: brought to live-NPPES freshness on open, still shown when the registry is silent, reconciled against its one required member.

actor "Person / Client" as P
participant "Gate\n(facade, transport only)" as GATE
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices main)" as UN
database "Registry\n(the one live map)" as REG
database "Repository\nsession, render ledger, page state" as REPO
participant "UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(FindCare satellite)" as PXY
participant "provider_detail\n(tool, required member)" as PDT
participant "NPPES\n(live query by NPI)" as NPPES
database "Provider record\ncollection" as DB
participant "Prose tool\n(authors the sentence)" as PROSE

note over UN, PROSE #fde68a
  OPEN ARCHITECTURAL QUESTION (not resolved here):
  whether authoring a user-facing sentence — the summary, the
  not-found line, the timeout line — is the UtteranceManager's OWN
  scope, or a SEPARATE "Prose" tool as drawn. Three approved
  requirements place prose and the manufacture path inside the
  UtteranceManager; the registry instance also carries a "Prose"
  route. The architecture will not move a requirement; which stands
  is the operator's to say. Drawn one way only to be concrete.
end note

P -> GATE : click a provider card's link\n{ session_token, head, params(openNpi) }
activate GATE
note over GATE
  A click, not an utterance. The gate collects the session token,
  the HTTP head, and the parameters, each if present, and hands
  them on. It is the single client entrance; it owns no route
  and verifies nothing.
end note
GATE -> UN : navigate(session_token, head, params)
activate UN
deactivate GATE

note right of UN
  TRIAGE by declared proof. Five ways a call may arrive:
  tool_to_tool (none), client_sessioned (session_token),
  third_party_callback (api_key), static_witness (none),
  internal_callback (our_signature). A session token is
  present -> this is a client_sessioned arrival. The
  UniversalNavigator is the only node that takes external traffic.
end note
UN -> REPO : verify session_token, advance the nonce
REPO --> UN : session ok

note right of UN
  DETERMINE THE PAGE from the live registry map: openNpi names a
  record whose entity is an individual -> the individualProvider page.
  provider_detail is a VIEW / MEMBER of that page, never a page itself.
  The UN holds no data; the map is the registry, page state a repo row.
end note
UN -> REG : read the live map for this env
REG --> UN : pages, members, required_members, may_call
UN -> REPO : page state = individualProvider page shows this NPI

note right of UN
  OPEN THE RENDER LEDGER. Record the required member for this
  detail-open as the expectation and race the completeness budget:
    members          = { provider_detail, prose }
    required_members = { provider_detail }
    budget           = completeness.render_timeout_seconds
end note
UN -> REPO : record ledger expectation { provider_detail }, start the budget

alt provider_detail returns within the budget
  UN -> PXY : dispatch provider_detail(openNpi)\nacross the wire (tool_to_tool, our_signature signed out)
  activate PXY
  PXY -> PDT : relay locally (function call)
  activate PDT

  PDT -> NPPES : query by NPI (live freshness on open)
  activate NPPES
  NPPES --> PDT : live record, or nothing
  deactivate NPPES

  alt the registry answered
    alt the NPI is an individual
      PDT -> DB : read the stored record
      DB --> PDT : record as we hold it
      PDT -> PDT : start from OUR record; apply only the registry's fields\n(identity, credentials, taxonomies, every address, licenses,\nother identifiers, active state — never an organization attribute)
      opt the freshness merge changed something real
        PDT -> DB : replace the record, read it back
        DB --> PDT : the record as now stored
        note right of PDT
          Whether this per-open freshness write targets the SERVED
          collection or a non-served store is the open two-writers
          question (C4/C5: served-data writers). Not settled here.
        end note
      end
    else the NPI is not an individual
      PDT -> PROSE : author "provider not found"
      PROSE --> PDT : the not-found sentence
      note right of PDT
        No Provider Detail is shown for an NPI the registry reports
        is not an individual; the user is told the provider was not found.
      end note
    end
  else the registry did not answer
    PDT -> DB : read the stored record
    DB --> PDT : record as we hold it (shown with no comparison)
    note right of PDT
      A detail is still shown when the source does not answer.
      Not answering leaves us no reason to doubt the record.
    end note
  end

  PDT -> PDT : build the panel\n- identity, credentials; every practice and business address, labelled and ordered\n- every license; insurance identifiers; active state\n- county info + urban marker (pipeline enrichment)\n- external research links to verify the provider independently
  PDT --> PXY : internal_callback { panel }  proof our_signature
  deactivate PDT
  PXY --> UN : internal_callback closes the required ledger entry
  deactivate PXY

  UN -> REPO : close the ledger entry for provider_detail
  UN -> UN : RECONCILE — every required member closed;\nserial deterministic merge of returning documents\n(a parameter/state conflict RAISES -> on_conflict)
  opt prose member
    UN -> PROSE : author the panel's summary, with the facts
    activate PROSE
    PROSE --> UN : the user-facing sentence
    deactivate PROSE
  end
  UN --> GATE : the reconciled provider panel

else the budget expires first  (on_timeout)
  UN -> PROSE : author the layman on_timeout explanation
  activate PROSE
  PROSE --> UN : "we could not bring this provider up in time — please try again"
  deactivate PROSE
  UN --> GATE : respond anyway, the page unrendered
  note right of UN
    The completeness timeout races the callback. On expiry the UN
    responds in layman's terms, instrumented with timings at a
    severity matching impact.
  end note

else provider_detail dies or never calls back  (on_missing_required)
  UN -> UN : render ledger RAISES — the one required member is missing;\ncatch, classify, log with timings
  UN --> GATE : ChatHealthyException surfaced
  note right of UN
    Every throw ends in a UniversalNavigator; the proxy re-raises.
    A required member that dies or never returns leaves the page
    unreconcilable.
  end note
end

[<-- GATE : the one stream the gate writes
deactivate UN
GATE --> P : the provider detail as the registry reports it now
deactivate GATE

@enduml
